Insertion at Head — Revision

To insert a node at the head of a singly linked list, create a new node with value X, make the new node point to the current head using newNode.next = head, then update head to newNode and return head. This works for both a non-empty and an empty list because if head == null, newNode.next simply becomes null.

Time: O(1) — only a few pointer operations are performed.
Auxiliary Space: O(1) — only one new node is created.


code
======================================
import java.util.*;

class ListNode {
    public int data;
    public ListNode next;

    ListNode() {
        data = 0;
        next = null;
    }

    ListNode(int x) {
        data = x;
        next = null;
    }

    ListNode(int x, ListNode next) {
        data = x;
        this.next = next;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public ListNode insertAtHead(ListNode head, int X) {

        // Create a new node with value X
        ListNode newNode = new ListNode(X);

        // Connect the new node to the old head
        newNode.next = head;

        // Make the new node the new head
        head = newNode;

        // Return the new head
        return head;
    }
}
